---
description: Testing and evaluation rules
globs: ["**/*.test.*", "**/test_*.py", "evals/**"]
alwaysApply: false
---
- Unit-test: guardrails, schema parsing/retry, permission checks, sync/idempotency, auth.
- Evals (not unit tests) cover agent quality: each agent has a dataset in `evals/datasets/`.
- A prompt or model change must not reduce any agent's eval pass rate; CI enforces the thresholds in `docs/evals.md`.
- Red-team dataset must pass 100% (every attack blocked or neutralised) before release.
- Tests use recorded/mocked model responses by default; live-model evals run in the eval job only.
